    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we need to first determine the length of one of its sides. According to the problem, the length of one side of the square can be expressed in two different ways: $4x-15$ meters and $20-3x$ meters. Since both expressions represent the same length, we can set them equal to each other and solve for $x$:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n4x-15 &= 20-3x \\\\\n7x &= 35 \\\\\nx &= 5\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow that we know the value of $x$, we can substitute it back into either expression to find the length of one side of the square. Let's use $4x-15$:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n4(5)-15 &= 20-3(5) \\\\\n20-15 &= 20-15 \\\\\n5 &= 5\n\\end{align*}\n\nThe length of one side of the square is 5 meters. To find the area, we simply square this length:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Area} &= 5^2 \\\\\n&= 25\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is $\\boxed{25}$ square meters.",
